{
 "result": "maze.py is an unrolled flat-bytearray BFS. It pads the grid with a '#' border, finds S and E with bytes.find, and expands frontier lists level by level, marking visited cells as '#'. It returns the distance when E is reached, or -1. It passes the public samples (2008, -1, 78). The unrolled neighbour loop was adopted as a +17% win over the previous body (4.063 vs 3.458). I am stopping here rather than spending more energy on a further change that would need more than 8% to count.",
